    "lawCode": "Amd §394-c, Gen Bus L (as proposed in S.1759-B & A.1057-C)",
    "lawSection": "General Business Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S778\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general business law, in relation to certain\nprovisions of online dating services\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2024, c.603, to provide technical\nfixes, clarify the definition of fraud ban and establish data deletion\nrequirements.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by modifying the defi-\nnition of fraud ban to include using a false identity, and adding\nprovisions allowing for the retention of data as required by law or to\ncomply with a judicial court order. The legislation additionally makes\ntechnical fixes for clarity.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 603 of the Laws of 2024. S.1759-B and\nA.1057-C both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in January\nand May 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the general business law, in\nrelation to certain provisions of online dating services, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S.1759-B and A.1057-C, takes effect.\n",
